A lone ':' as a statement, a ':' with a space before a keyword name, and
a ':' at end of file. The validator must report each without panicking,
and the formatter must not glue the colon onto a neighboring token.
-- input.ssl --
:DECLARE nCount;
:;
nCount := 1;
: IF nCount > 0;
nCount += 1;
:ENDIF;
:
-- format --
:DECLARE nCount;
:;
nCount := 1;
: IF nCount > 0;
nCount += 1;
:ENDIF;
:
-- diagnostics --
2:1-2:2 error unexpected_token: Unexpected ':' - a colon starts a keyword (written with no space, ':IF') or follows the object in a member access
4:1-4:2 error unexpected_token: Unexpected ':' - a colon starts a keyword (written with no space, ':IF') or follows the object in a member access (remove the space: ':IF')
6:1-6:7 error unmatched_block_end: Unexpected ':ENDIF' without matching block start
7:1-7:2 error unexpected_token: Unexpected ':' - a colon starts a keyword (written with no space, ':IF') or follows the object in a member access
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
2:1-2:2 error unexpected_token: Unexpected ':' - a colon starts a keyword (written with no space, ':IF') or follows the object in a member access
4:1-4:2 error unexpected_token: Unexpected ':' - a colon starts a keyword (written with no space, ':IF') or follows the object in a member access (remove the space: ':IF')
6:1-6:7 error unmatched_block_end: Unexpected ':ENDIF' without matching block start
7:1-7:2 error unexpected_token: Unexpected ':' - a colon starts a keyword (written with no space, ':IF') or follows the object in a member access
